UPDATE companies SET description='Williston Woodworks was founded in 1952 in Williston, North Dakota, before Second Avenue West was paved. The company incorporated in 1955, initially producing residential cabinets and wooden boats for the newly formed Lake Sakakawea. In 1964, the growing business moved to a larger facility on Second Avenue, and in 1983 it relocated to its current 15,000-square-foot shop West.

The firm designs, manufactures, and installs custom kitchen, bath, and specialty cabinetry, along with countertops and custom stairways. Its full-service process covers measuring, detailed space layout, fabrication, delivery, and professional installation. The shop serves both residential and commercial clients, producing custom casework for banks, hospitals, nursing homes, and office complexes.

Williston Woodworks coordinates with local builders, electricians, and plumbers to manage entire project scopes, from new construction to renovations.

