UPDATE companies SET description='Woodlore, LLC operates from Fairfield in Rockbridge County, Virginia. The company was founded on the principle of salvaging local trees that have fallen due to storms or urbanization, rather than harvesting live timber. No founding year or founder names are publicly disclosed, and ownership structure is not specified.

The company mills salvaged logs into natural live edge slabs and fabricates custom furniture including tables, desks, benches, mantels, countertops, and bar tops. All processing—from log salvage to finishing—occurs under one roof. Woodlore also provides portable sawmill services using a Wood-Mizer LT50 Wide hydraulic sawmill, and kiln drying via an iDRY vacuum kiln with a capacity of 13 feet long by 48 inches wide by 55 inches thick (stickered lumber pile), handling up to 2,000 board feet per cycle. Drying time averages approximately one week per inch of lumber thickness. Facility size, employee count, and annual production volumes are not disclosed.

The company’s stated mission is to give new life to dead trees, providing organic furnishings and artisan materials while caring for the environment. Woodlore emphasizes honesty, integrity, and quality craftsmanship, and differentiates itself by keeping the entire process—from salvage to finished product—in-house, allowing clients to participate in wood selection and design.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tree salvaging", "Live edge slab milling", "Custom furniture building", "Portable sawmill services", "Kiln drying (vacuum kiln)", "Custom steel leg fabrication", "Custom wooden leg fabrication", "Design consultation", "Slab selection assistance"], "industries": ["Custom furniture", "Live edge slab supply", "Tree salvage and reclamation", "Portable sawmill services", "Kiln drying services", "Woodworking", "Interior design", "Architectural millwork"], "materials": ["Salvaged local hardwoods", "Steel (for legs)", "Wood (for legs)"], "equipment": ["Wood-Mizer LT50 Wide Hydraulic Portable Sawmill", "iDRY vacuum kiln"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Kiln drying: approximately one week per inch of lumber thickness", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Whole process from log salvage to finished product under one roof", "Salvages trees instead of harvesting; partners with VDOT, landowners, and arborists", "iDRY vacuum kiln with 2,000 board foot capacity", "Portable sawmill services on-site or at their facility", "Client involvement in wood selection and design"], "facts_used": ["Location: Fairfield, Rockbridge County, Virginia -> db", "Business model: salvages fallen trees, mills live edge slabs, builds custom furniture -> /", "Products: tables, desks, benches, mantels, countertops, bar tops -> /", "Process: whole process from log salvage to finishing under one roof -> /", "Portable sawmill: Wood-Mizer LT50 Wide Hydraulic Portable Sawmill -> /services", "Kiln drying: iDRY vacuum kiln, capacity 13ft L x 48in W x 55in T, max 2000 board feet, drying time ~1 week per inch -> /services", "Tree salvage partners: VDOT, local land owners, arborists -> /services", "Custom steel or wooden legs offered -> /", "Client involvement in selection and design -> /", "Mission: offer new life to dead trees, environmentally conscious -> /", "Values: honesty, integrity, quality craftsmanship -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Woodlore LLC is an environmentally conscious business which salvages local trees that have fallen from storms and urbanization. Instead of harvesting trees, we save dead or diseased trees from being processed into non recyclable products such as firewood, and mill them into natural live edge slabs. We sell local wood and build custom furniture.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='woodlore-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Woodside Industries Inc is based in Cavalier, North Dakota. Founded in 2001, the company began with local kitchen projects before expanding into custom commercial cabinetry.

The company operates a 30,000-square-foot facility where it designs, manufactures, finishes, and installs custom commercial cabinetry, architectural millwork, and industrial casework. Its capabilities include healthcare-grade cabinetry, an automated finishing line, and a range of countertop materials.

Woodside serves healthcare, multi-unit residential, education, government, hospitality, banking, dental, retail, airport, and restaurant sectors. Past clients include Langlas & Associates for school projects in Montana and North Dakota, with completed projects in Fargo, Bozeman, Grand Rapids, Grand Forks, and Ponderay.

