UPDATE companies SET description='3 Crowns Apparel Services operates as a vertically integrated apparel design and manufacturing facility in Brooklyn, New York.

The company provides end-to-end development and production services under one roof: product strategy and planning, pattern making, sample development, sourcing of fabrics, trims, and hardware, and small-batch manufacturing. Master tailors on staff enable production of tailored clothing, gowns, ready-to-wear, activewear, and children''s apparel. The facility handles pre-production build setup, including spec review, measurement alignment, and component specification, through to production readiness with detailed material requirements.

3 Crowns serves emerging and established apparel brands of any size, as well as independent designers seeking to turn concepts into production-ready products. Its consulting arm draws on over 18 years of fashion industry experience spanning visual merchandising, creative services, design, buying, retail development, and business management.

The studio differentiates itself through its commitment to craft and partnership, offering a full scope of services that bridge design and manufacturing. By keeping development and production in-house, it aims to reduce barriers for smaller brands and ensure ethical, transparent operations from strategy to shelf.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product strategy & planning", "Pattern making", "Sample development", "Fabric and trim sourcing", "Hardware sourcing (zippers, buttons, thread, elastic, hooks/eyes)", "Cut-and-sew manufacturing", "Pre-production build setup", "Production readiness consulting", "Apparel design consulting"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Fashion", "Ready-to-wear", "Activewear", "Children''s apparel", "Tailored clothing", "Gowns"], "materials": ["Apparel fabrics", "Trims", "Hardware (zippers, buttons, thread, elastic, hooks/eyes)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated facility in Brooklyn handling design through manufacturing", "Master tailors on staff for diverse apparel categories", "18+ years of fashion industry consulting experience", "Small-batch development and production under one roof", "Focus on equitable, accessible fashion for independent designers"], "facts_used": ["Location: Brooklyn, NY -> db", "Vertically integrated apparel design and manufacturing facility -> /about", "Services: product strategy, pattern making, sample development, sourcing, manufacturing -> /", "Manufactures tailored clothing, gowns, ready-to-wear, activewear, children''s apparel -> /about", "Master tailors on staff -> /about", "Consulting led by professionals with 18+ years industry experience -> /about", "Mission: make fashion equitable and accessible for independent designers/emerging brands -> /about", "Commitment to craft, partnership, ethically run -> /about", "Small-batch development and manufacturing studio -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "3Crowns is a vertically integrated apparel design and manufacturing facility located in Brooklyn NY.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='3-crowns-apparel-services' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='3-V Distributing Inc. is based in Conrad, Montana. Founded in 1978 by John VanDyke, the company began as a seller, distributor, and installer of aluminum grain bodies produced by ITB Inc. VanDyke recognized a regional need for quality truck equipment and built the business around that gap. Ownership passed to his son, Jordan VanDyke, who now serves as president, keeping the operation family-run.

The company distributes and installs a range of truck and trailer equipment, including grain bodies, dump bodies, flatbeds, landscape bodies, lift axles, suspensions, bale beds, hoists, tarp systems, snow and ice equipment, and hydraulic systems. It carries product lines from manufacturers such as ITB, Henderson, Crysteel, DuraClass, Rugby, Deweze, Henke, Force America, Cirus, Buyers Products, CPI, Rol Oyl, Pintle Hitch, and SwapLoader. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

The VanDyke family’s own farming background informs their product selection, and they emphasize hands-on familiarity with the equipment they supply.

